Pinned upstream: SnowflakePowered/librashader 07ac790cdb9826f37cf8e1daf5011f03e3c4daa7

Own every active pipeline layout/descriptor pool/set layout, with partial-constructor
cleanup. Free pipeline caches and any partial pipelines on pipeline creation errors.
Own temporary initialization command pools before fallible setup; after a submit
error, require successful idle or DEVICE_LOST before releasing submitted resources.
If idle cannot prove completion, deliberately retain those resources rather than
free objects that the GPU may still be using.

Register per-frame input/output image views immediately with the existing deferred
residual owner, including draw/allocation errors. Own buffers/images before memory
allocation or binding, release handles before their memory, and postpone ManuallyDrop
until the mapped-buffer constructor has succeeded. These are unique owners: no new
Clone/Copy implementation and no second manual free of descriptor sets. The existing
caller remains responsible for GPU completion before normal chain destruction.
LUT support and shader algorithms are unchanged.

